    "c19": {
      "anchor": "hosting#markdown-2",
      "kind": "markdown",
      "label": "11. Hosting",
      "excerpt": "People's accounts: the org makes one for each person who joins, as ana.spell.spa",
      "text": "this is personal, what is this for spell-created accounts?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-02T03:26:11.953Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "People's accounts: the org makes one for each person who joins, as ana.spell.spaces, so a group's size decides the size of its host. An account holds that person's posts and comments.",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-02T03:26:17.935Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-02T03:27:13.708Z",
          "html": "<p>Good catch.  For an account the org makes, people see <code>ana@rs</code>, and underneath it's <code>ana.rs.spell.spaces</code>, or <code>ana.their-own-domain.org</code> for an org with its own domain.  An AT Protocol name has to be a web address, so the org goes in as its own level.  <code>ana.spell.spaces</code> is left for personal accounts.  It's in the doc now.</p>\n<p>Not checked:  whether the host we buy can give each org its own level like that.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-02T03:27:01.021Z"
      }
    }
